[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged every "wrong day" report into one ticket and called it one bug
with one fix queued. Read report by report, it holds more than one problem, and each one has its
own ticket. Engineering has since closed #4471; the table shows how each ticket closed.

<Callout>
Closed. <code>parser</code> is fixed. <code>hint</code> will not be fixed: booking-v3 is retired.
The one-day moves are merged into <code>parser</code>, where the desk files them.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

## The problems

**`parser` — the shared parser read every date month first.** Every tenant on file writes the
day first, so a day-first date came out with day and month swapped: through the app, by email
and through the booking-v2 form. Engineering fixed this one.

**`hint` — booking-v3 prints a month-first hint under its date field.** Only tenants on
booking-v3, and only reports through that form. People type what the hint tells them, month
first; the form then reads the date the tenant's way, day first. The result looks the same as
`parser`, so subject-line merging put it in #4471, but the parser fix does not touch it.
Engineering will not fix it: the booking-v3 form is retired.

**`shift` — the date lands a day early.** Day and month are not swapped: the weekday moves back
by one, a client in another time zone gets a different day for the same meeting, an invite
arrives before the booking was made. That is a date stored or sent as a midnight time and
converted across time zones. Neither code path in `causes.ts` produces it, so the cause table on
#4471 files these under the tenant's cause with a footnote. The table above counts them the
desk's way: where they are filed, and again as `shift`. Their ticket is merged into `parser`'s.

## Why the merge hid them

- Merging by subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) cannot see
  any of this: every problem arrives as "wrong day".
- Intake tags come from the reporter's browser, not the tenant. The table counts by tenant and
  form; compare its two columns.
- The cause table on #4471 picks the biggest group as the ticket's cause and marks the rest
  "no ticket of its own". They have tickets now.

## What to watch

- The parser fix does not reach a time-zone shift. If one-day moves keep coming after it, reopen
  the `shift` ticket.
- Decision 0001 still merges on subject alone, so the next incident will hide its problems the
  same way. A new decision record should replace it.

